WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.350
Click, click, click.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.570
Good, looks like you didn't give me a fake number.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.780
The first mail I got from Ryuushi-san was...

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.290
It's Ryuuko!

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.120
Click, click, click.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.290
Ryuushi-san.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.710
Hey!

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.340
Your hair is all straightened out.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.180
Don't look!

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.910
Hello there.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.700
The infamous Maekawa-san, who saved you from the teacher's long speech, is here.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.090
The end of the year assembly ended early thanks to her heat stroke.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.330
Are you okay?

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.520
My semicircular canals aren't in top form yet, but I'm managing.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.410
I was told my body retains heat
more than the average person

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.220
I don't handle saunas and long baths very well.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.670
Is this a new experiment or ritual for you two?

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.500
We just exchanged our numbers.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.420
Oh? Maybe I'll exchange mine with you guys too.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:16.660
By the way, does Touwa have a phone?

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.100
Well, I don't think so.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.850
Oh, she doesn't.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.810
That didn't count!

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.690
You didn't hear that meanie Ryuuko-san!

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:26.980
The past, begone!

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.560
You have it hard too, eh, Ryuushi?

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.860
It's Ryuuko.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.990
Or as an athlete, maybe it motivates you to have a rival?

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.330
Why you say!

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:41.740
I mean...

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.490
What you say?

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.170
It finally feels like summer's here, now that the break has begun.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:55.970
Right.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:59.930
At first, it feels like forever until the end of August.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.180
But then it's over before you know it.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.220
I still have club activities.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.390
And matches!

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.350
I might get to play this year!

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.360
Great!

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.480
I might go cheer for you!

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.190
Y-You're coming?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:16.990
You'll cheer for me?

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.740
Well, yes... Unless you don't want me to?

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.490
Time out. Ryuuko-chan, it's your turn!

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.240
Substitute for Mikki!

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.790
Niwa-kun!

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.040
I-I think I'll get to play, so please come if you can.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.130
Roger.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.510
All right!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.550
By the way...

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.390
Are you the type who's too lazy to exchange a lot of messages?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.680
No, I like them.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.350
Then, I'll mail you like crazy!

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.520
You can send tons to my cell too!

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.450
Okay! I can't think of many things to say, though.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.320
Don't you underestimate me!

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.080
I have an unique personality and millions of conversation topics in my mind!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.500
You're in for a journey to discover Ryuuko-san this summer!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.210
Got it?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.880
We split up at the intersection,

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.210
as we usually do.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.340
I'll gaze at the bridge Ryuushi-san is about to cross...

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.840
while she sticks out her tongue.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.220
It's been our routine since a week before finals, when club activities were suspended.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.390
Let's make it a fun summer break, Niwa-kun!

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:06.320
Makoto-chwaan-chan!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.280
Yes?

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.320
Baboo!

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.580
Guwashi!

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.450
<i>That</i> "Makoto-chan"?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:15.040
You're so cold, Mako-kun!

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.580
If you're so cold to me,

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:23.590
my visit-summer-festival-together-then-grab-a-

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.840
Totally fall apart!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.340
Save your sleep talking for when you're asleep.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.180
Don't forget to bring in the laundry.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.970
Okay, fine, fine.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.690
Why?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.030
Hello?

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.860
Did you get my message?

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.030
I did. Is that why you're calling me?

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.450
Yep! Do you like baseball?

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.700
I played a little in elementary school.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:56.120
Well, we do welcome beginners...

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.330
are you willing to join an amateur baseball team?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.210
Are you scouting for the team?

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:06.470
I only help out during the summer, but we play by the riverbank early in the morning.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.050
Early morning baseball, huh?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.430
There's more to it, though.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.600
What do you mean?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.730
I mean there's a greater purpose to it.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.180
You don't have to come every time.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.060
Just help us out when we don't have enough players.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.940
I guess I could.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.990
Thanks, that'd be great.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.610
You should've just asked me in school.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.870
Come on, transfer student.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.790
I'm not insensitive enough to mention that in front of Ryuushi.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.410
Okay...

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.170
Yo.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:46.550
Yo.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.220
You're not wrapped in futon today.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:54.970
What?

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.020
Telescope.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.270
I can see that.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:06:59.980
Sky.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.690
Oh, I think I know what you're getting at.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.810
Notebook.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.360
Stargazing?

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.570
Yes!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.080
Would the cousin like to try too?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.250
You're asking me to join you?

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.330
Well, okay.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.420
I have nothing else to do so I'll join you.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.590
Welcome.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.840
Why does that lead you to offer me a dust cloth?

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.060
Out!

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.320
Close one, transfer student.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.690
Was that sarcasm?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:49.690
No, no!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.990
I'm impressed you got a piece of that pitch.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.620
It's your first day, don't be disappointed.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:03.870
Strike!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.630
She goes to our school, right?

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.130
Yep, the softball team's captain.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.920
Her name is... Hanazawa, I think.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.300
Did your costume remind you of that name?

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.760
It did.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.640
What is that costume, anyway?

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.560
Skipjack tuna.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.310
There's no need to obsess over it. I'm not Nakajima, after all.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.810
Exclusively for pole fishing.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.900
Three outs, change!

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.320
I can't tell the difference.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.070
Let's go.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.450
Oh, right.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.740
Our pitcher is Maekawa's dad.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.330
My friend the transfer student.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.910
His name is... uh...

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:43.710
Shiwa-kun.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.580
Friend, guy friend, mumble-mumble...

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:50.590
He must have mistaken me for a Poke-something creature, with three evolutionary stages.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.090
Ball, take your base!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.310
Our pitcher's throws are hard to hit, aren't they?

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.020
Yeah.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.810
I can never hit them.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.480
When she pitches, you can see up her skirt from the left-hand batter's box.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.110
Seriously?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.110
I'm just messing with you.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.740
Strike!

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.410
I'm Nakajima. You're the transfer student, right?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.660
You're in my school?

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.120
Yep.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.210
Why are you playing here?

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.920
I guess because Maekawa-san asked me to.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.880
Oh, you two are pretty close?

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.670
But, the transfer student...

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.550
Well, never mind.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.760
You live by the shopping district, right?

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.590
Since you're on their team.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.810
I think I'm in the city side.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.890
Shopping district side and city side, huh?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.310
This city has the rapidly growing "city side",

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.520
and the shopping district with old buildings.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.270
It seems there's a certain divide between these two.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:58.820
Maekawa-san is in the peculiar position of living on the city side, though her parents have a bar in the shopping district.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:02.120
In case you're curious, Ryuushi-san is as city-side as it gets.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.040
Is there rivalry between the two sides?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.330
Depends.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:11.340
I don't really care, but some people get bullied because of that.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.550
Oh.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.010
That's why we play baseball.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.890
It's kind of awkward talking to me, huh?

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.970
Well, I guess...

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:27.890
I somehow knew it'd get awkward if we talked about anything serious.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.820
Out!

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.830
The game ended after six innings, per the rules of amateur baseball.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.410
I hear it's customary for the losing team to clean up the field.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.040
Hi, is Meme doing well?

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:58.510
If by "doing well" you mean a forty-year-old lady acting like a preschool girl, then yes.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.180
Has she said anything about me?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.930
Nope, nothing at all.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.810
Oh, eel.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:09.890
Just leftovers from the bar.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.650
A reward for the hard-working transfer student.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.360
I barely hit the ball.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.400
No, you hit it in front of you.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.820
Well, it would've been foul if it went behind me.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.320
That's not what I meant.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:24.450
You shy boy.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.160
I bet it's from Ryuushi.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.700
I'm not telling.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:38.920
Don't you want to make her burst into laughter?

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:44.850
If I put any effort into it, Ryuushi-san goes out of control trying to outdo me.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.890
Pickled eggplant or salted cod roe.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:59.780
They're yours. Feel free to keep them or give them away.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.110
These are precious rice balls...

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:06.700
But if this were a conversation with Meme-san...

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.870
Mako-kun is in a rebellious phase!

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.000
He has a thing for his auntie, yet he suppresses his adolescent desires,

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.250
so his pent-up teenage lust exploded and he went around sniffing my things!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.840
What a noisy imagination!

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.470
You sure I can have it?

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.600
Sure, Hanazawa-sa—

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.310
Thank you, Isono-kun.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.020
Thank this girl next to me...

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.480
Thanks, Maekawa.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.980
Don't mention it.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:37.820
How is it?

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:41.240
It's good enough to make me want to marry into your family.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:44.490
Then my dad will have to get a divorce!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.240
Are you Maekawa's boyfriend?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.250
Hear that, transfer student?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:59.340
The transfer student will be wearing a mackerel costume before long.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.970
That would be the worst coupling on a whole new dimension!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.470
Captain!

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.550
I have to get to our morning practice.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.550
Thanks.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:14.230
Our team can't win without beating Hanazawa's pitching.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.230
That's probably impossible.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.770
The team's future is in the hands of the transfer student!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:22.650
What are you expecting from an amateur like me?

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.530
We're all counting on you!

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:29.830
Even if you're not that good, you should still have confidence in yourself!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.750
That's just not my personality.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.370
True, you have a point there.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.460
The transfer student always starts out being skeptical.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.470
Will you join us again for baseball?

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:50.010
If I can have your rice balls again.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:06.900
Yo.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.910
Good morning, the cousin.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.830
Where were you?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:13.950
On the riverbank.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.040
I was playing baseball.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.330
Baseball?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.420
What?

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.550
Tonight too?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.130
Fine, fine!

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:25.760
I'll join you.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:33.600
The cousin, is baseball fun?

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:37.940
Are you interested in baseball?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:59.120
Yay, Meme-chin swept the vote among youths in the city's popularity contest.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.580
ZZZzzzZZZ

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.840
You made up that contest.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.750
Good morning, Mako-tan.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.460
Call me something normal.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.300
Mako, Mako, tan-tan.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:11.010
That was an impossible request for an old lady whose weirdness is something normal.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.090
Sorry.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:15.600
There are some things people just can't do.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.480
Like flying with a bicycle, or being an alien,

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.730
or becoming a hero in amateur baseball.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.230
It's mentally healthier to not get my hopes up.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:30.990
The hottest girl in the city, Meme-chin, is a wife who lost her husband!

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:32.990
Your forehead is all red.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.330
The cousin!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.210
It's time for stargazing.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.960
Oh, okay. It's that time already?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.920
What's with the futon?

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.260
Anti-mosquito.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.470
Anti-mosquito?

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:57.560
Good idea, let's go!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.390
Go, only as far as the backyard.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.810
Erio is currently not allowed to travel too far at night.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:08.730
No, Erio. The city at night...

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:15.280
has hungry wolves preying on cute little lambs like you!

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.200
What was the meaning of that glance during the pause?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.040
Okay, let's watch the stars or whatever!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.330
Go, be free!

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:32.840
It seems she finally realized that she won't get mosquito bites but can't see anything wrapped in futon.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.850
Give up and get yourself out of that.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.100
The cousin commanded me to strip.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:43.850
You don't have to strip.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.560
Would you rather stare at your futon all night?

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.360
Good!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.870
I got to see it again tonight.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.290
I got to see her smile again.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.620
I'll take that remark of mine to the grave.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.880
We can see something even more amazing soon!

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.550
When are you appearing on TV, cousin?

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.890
Who are you talking about?

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.060
You're playing baseball.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:26.230
They would rather air high school baseball than us, the Riverbanks.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.900
Is the cousin talking about the amateur baseball team by the riverbank?

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.570
Yeah, we've seen it, remember?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.370
Are you on the shopping district's team?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.070
Yeah.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:43.580
Can I join you?

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.420
At baseball?

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.130
More like <i>baseball.</i>

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.340
<i><b>Baseball!</b></i>

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.590
Erio just said she wants to participate in a group activity.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:58.840
I want to rush into the house now, and report that to Meme-san...

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.350
I'll ask them.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.850
Thank you.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.770
Okay, I'll wait for you inside.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:10.400
What is it?

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:15.070
I thought I saw something glittering beside the moon.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:22.370
And so, I brought the girl who wanted to join.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.750
N-Nice to meet you... guys.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.410
Oh, she's Touwa's...

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:28.960
Oh, the futon...

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.380
Meme's daughter, huh?

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.460
Have you played baseball before?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:33.800
I play right field—

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.090
No prior experience.

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.630
Oh well, she can play right field.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.430
Good for you.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.430
What is that?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.100
Maekawa-san's cosplay buddy?

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.940
Nope, I don't recognize her.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.150
It's not a real spacesuit.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.030
Huh? I didn't call her today.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.320
Ah! It's Niwa-kun!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.200
Thanks.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.700
What an unexpected turn of events.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.460
Maekawa-san is here...

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.130
Touwa-san too, yet...

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:17.050
Niwa-kun excluded me from the group!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.220
Only me!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.010
No, no, it's not like that. Why are you here?

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.890
I'm practicing on my own.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.810
There's a basketball court in the park over there.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.680
Wow, you're pretty dedicated.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.850
Well, you know...

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.730
I have to play well if Niwa-kun's coming to cheer for me.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:42.610
Hi.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.570
Hi.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.620
Awkward relationship?

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.750
A-A friend.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.250
He's on the basketball team too,

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.120
Nakajima-kun.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:01.970
Geez.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:07.100
Ryuushi-san went to her basketball practice with her cranky walk.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:10.640
Half of it is an act to hide something from me.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:13.650
Strike!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:18.570
It does appear that a serious talk would lead to a heated argument.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:26.450
It's the bottom of the third, and number seven in the lineup, Touwa Erio, is at bat for the first time.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.330
Strike!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.630
Does Touwa even know the rules of baseball?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:38.550
I wonder.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.480
Are you all right?

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:09.790
Safe!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.800
It's not your fault.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:23.550
Probably.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:34.140
Sorry.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:36.140
Do- not- wor-ry.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.110
Why is this city filled with freaks?

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:43.150
What- is- this?

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:49.410
You don't have to enunciate your breathing too.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.290
You- seem- like- crea-tures- from- pla-net- Da-n-na-ri- Ka-pu-te.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:01.630
Are- you- in-volved- in- this- some-how?

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:04.380
And- what- a-bout- him?

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:06.300
Time out.

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.890
Sor-ry- to- keep- you- wai-ting. Bring- it!

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.890
Uh... just what are you?

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:21.520
I- am- an- es-per!

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:27.950
It's been a while, can I end the episode with this again?

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:29.200
I guess I can.

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:30.450
One word.

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:32.280
Fine.

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:05.840
Exchanging numbers with Ryuushi-san: +2

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:07.750
And with Maekawa-san too: +2

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:09.460
Going home from school with Ryuushi-san: +1

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:11.380
Amateur baseball in the early morning: +1

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:13.840
Striking out with Maekawa-san's dad: -1

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:15.760
Maekawa-san's rice ball: +1

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:19.310
Taking care of Erio, fewer things to worry about: -1

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:21.020
Cute Ryuushi-san: +2

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:23.940
Meeting a self-proclaimed esper: -3

00:24:23.940 --> 00:24:26.150
Current adolescence points total: +6

00:24:26.150 --> 00:24:28.440
Next time: The Girl Under the Eaves.

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:31.130
We- are- a-li-ens!
